  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://example.org/ontology/scholarly-discovery">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology"/>
    <rdfs:label>Scholarly discovery ontology profile</rdfs:label>
    <owl:versionInfo>4.0.1-draft</owl:versionInfo>
    <rdfs:comment>Existing vocabulary terms only. Embedded anonymous SHACL shapes record draft usage constraints; they do not redefine source properties' global domains/ranges. Logical consistency, CQ coverage and data conformance require separate evaluation.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>CQ_001: Given a publication PID, find all articles that cite it plus those cited in the publication itself.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>CQ_002: Given an author, return all documents where one of his/her work is cited.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>CQ_003a: Give me the references of all the available datasets that I can find in this federation of graphs.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>CQ_003b: Give me the list of identifiers of all the available datasets that I can find in this federation of graphs related to topic X and keywords Y.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>Modelling note: CQ_001 uses cito:cites and cito:isCitedBy for directed citations; both directions are required for the query result.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>Modelling note: CQ_002 uses schema:author to link authors to their works; author PIDs are handled via dcterms:identifier.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>Modelling note: CQ_003a and CQ_003b use dcat:Dataset for datasets and dcat:Catalog for the discovery catalogue; topics are represented as skos:Concept with dcterms:subject, keywords as dcat:keyword literals.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>Modelling note: dcterms:identifier is used for all resource PIDs; it is a literal string with no PID scheme constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>Modelling note: schema:ScholarlyArticle is preferred for scholarly articles in CQ_001; CreativeWork is the base class for all query results.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>UNRESOLVED OQ_02: CQ_001 requires a decision on whether to return citation direction with article identifiers; this affects the response format but is not covered by the ontology profile.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:comment>UNRESOLVED OQ_03: Keyword matching rules (all/any) and topic label matching for CQ_003b are application-level decisions, not ontology constraints.</rdfs:comment>
    <dcterms:description>Run metadata: {"catalogue_version": "2.0", "completion_source": "provider", "cq_coverage": "not_checked", "engine_version": "4.0.1", "generated_utc": "2026-11-03T08:25:22.623047+00:00", "input_sha256": {"catalogue": "18e15a83cf7f682c61750081e8103e53d8e3b037cf61751387520320cee41382", "cqs": "10f0d2b176f1046e2ab829187c81878169ffe5109493fcb4852922b445bf3f9a", "orsd": "c06366a6dc90c2bc95902ea535098c6e507dc59969ae44b97ca2d43df988d599", "prompt": "c841ea9106573adf011ac8c29bf7d788b0ecedf00370ed949b7565876ebc778e", "settings": "679f4f3a5008bd1fd427e5cd5b7e8641efb0133601088e406853d79181855453"}, "logical_consistency": "not_checked", "mode": "joint", "model": "qwen3:4b", "provider": "ollama", "shacl_data_validation": "not_checked"}</dcterms:description>
    <rdfs:seeAlso rdf:resource="https://sparontologies.github.io/cito/current/cito.html"/>
